CybNate

Parts of the agent instructions in app/src/main/assets/www/core.js (the general
guidelines, agent-spawning guidelines, code review guidelines and web research
guidance) are adapted from the Codebuff / Freebuff project
(https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff), Copyright 2025 Codebuff, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
The text was shortened and changed to match the tools available on Android.

Phase 1 safety work (approval before commands and file changes, untrusted tool results) follows ideas
that are common to agent tools, including the command approval flow described by hermes-agent
(NousResearch, MIT). No code was copied from that project.

Agent engine overhaul (system prompt structure, edit formats, verification rules). The following
open-source projects were studied. Ideas and, where stated, short adapted wording are used; no source
code of these projects is included in this app.

- OpenHands (All Hands AI, MIT): prompt section layout (ROLE, EFFICIENCY, FILE_SYSTEM_GUIDELINES,
  CODE_QUALITY, VERSION_CONTROL, PROBLEM_SOLVING_WORKFLOW, TROUBLESHOOTING, SECURITY), the
  str_replace_editor / execute_bash / finish tool names accepted as aliases, history condensation.
- SWE-agent / mini-swe-agent (Princeton NLP, MIT): edit-then-lint feedback loop, compact tool output,
  reproduce-before-fix workflow.
- Aider (Aider AI, Apache-2.0): SEARCH/REPLACE block format, layered fuzzy matching of edits,
  repository map idea, lint and test after every edit.
- Cline and Roo Code (Apache-2.0): ask_followup_question / attempt_completion end-of-turn tools,
  apply_diff format, mode-style slash commands, @file mentions, context condensing.
- Codebuff (Apache-2.0): file-picker / basher / editor / reviewer / thinker helper roles (see above).
- Pyodide (MPL-2.0) is downloaded at build time and shipped unmodified. Packages installed by the
  built-in npm come from the jsDelivr CDN at run time and keep their own licences.
